// Syncthing ignore rules shared by every device that syncs this Solaris checkout.
// Each device's .stignore (never synced by Syncthing, gitignored here) is one line,
// `#include .stglobalignore`, plus any device-only rules after it. Edit this file, not the
// per-device copies. Syncthing treats a missing include file as an error, so a new device needs
// this file in place before its folder starts. Do not ignore .memory/ : that layer is how a
// session on one machine sees operating memory written on another.

(?d).DS_Store
(?d).Spotlight-V100
(?d).Trashes
(?d)Thumbs.db
(?d)desktop.ini

(?d)**/.venv
(?d)**/.venv*
(?d)**/node_modules
(?d)**/.npm

(?d)**/__pycache__
(?d)**/*.pyc
(?d)**/*.pyo
(?d)**/*.pyd
(?d)**/.pytest_cache
(?d)**/.ruff_cache
(?d)**/.mypy_cache
(?d)**/*.egg-info

(?d)/.tmp
(?d)/.tools

(?d)**/*.nosync
(?d)**/*.noSync
(?d)**/.playwright*
(?d)**/dist
(?d)**/build

// Each machine keeps its own git clone. No (?d): a directory deleted on another device must not
// take this machine's clone (and any unpushed commits) with it.
**/.git

// Project data and run outputs (the ai-pack's local-only `__data/` and `__out/`): large,
// regenerated, and kept on the machine that produced them. No (?d), for the same reason.
**/__data
**/__out

// Per-machine runtime (gitignored; tokens and local overrides). No (?d): deleting a copy here
// must not delete another machine's.
/.mcp.json
/.cursor/mcp.json
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.claude/agents

// Conflict copies stay on the machine that lost. Session start union-merges interactions.jsonl
// copies locally; other leftovers are reported, not synced.
**/*sync-conflict-*
